          "worked": "Since $0<\\frac{1}{a}<1$, the curve has domain $x>0$ and is decreasing. Equivalently,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_{1/a}(x)&=\\frac{\\log_a(x)}{-1}\\\\\\log_{1/a}(x)&=-\\log_a(x)\\end{align*}$$\nDiagram (II).",
